<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A button that opens a list of options - pick one, or several.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/select)

<%= embed UI::SelectPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Select(name: "fruit", default_value: "apple") do
  SelectTrigger(aria_label: "Fruit") { SelectValue(placeholder: "Pick a fruit") }
  SelectContent do
    SelectItem(value: "apple") { "Apple" }
    SelectItem(value: "orange") { "Orange" }
  end
end
```

The root holds the value and the shared `size:` / `variant:`. `SelectTrigger` is styled like an
[Input](<%= page_path(:input) %>) and shows `SelectValue`. `SelectContent` opens in the browser's top layer (the
Popover API), so no `overflow: hidden` ancestor clips it; by default it opens over the trigger with the selected item
aligned to it (`align_item_with_trigger: false` opens below). A visually hidden input submits the value and carries
`required:`, so the Select validates in a [Field](<%= page_path(:field) %>). For long lists users need to search, use
a [Combobox](<%= page_path(:combobox) %>).

